@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>Privacy - TheBluesland</PageTitle>
<PageMetadata
    Title="Privacy - TheBluesland"
    Description="How TheBluesland handles data: no account, no unnecessary personal data collection, and a click-to-load Spotify embed."
    CanonicalPath="/privacy"
    ImagePath="/og-image.png" />

<article class="privacy">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    @* Placeholder copy (US-008): final wording pending Mehmet's review, same as the draft
       curator notes under content/playlists pending US-015. Kept short but readable so the page
       is never an empty shell. *@
    <p>
        TheBluesland does not require an account and does not collect personal data beyond what
        your browser or hosting provider sends as part of any web request.
    </p>
    <p>
        Playlist detail pages can embed a Spotify player. That embed is only loaded after you
        choose to click "listen" (click-to-load, see US-010); until then, no Spotify iframe or
        Spotify cookie is present on the page. Once loaded, Spotify's own privacy policy applies
        to that embedded player.
    </p>
    <p>This page is a placeholder - final legal wording will replace this text before launch.</p>
</article>
